From 8a61520fde79de440f8bcb02cc35b968b6ba7303 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:14:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/43] drm/gma500: add SGX MMU page tables for the SGX545
 driver

The SGX545 driver needs page directories of its own: one for the firmware
and one per future GPU address space. Add sgx_mmu, a small two-level page
table manager whose directory and table pages are mapped uncached, so the
entries are in memory when the BIF walks them and no CPU cache flush is
needed before a kick. Live entries are never silently replaced. KUnit checks
the PDE and PTE encoding and a mapping across a page-table boundary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/Makefile       |   4 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgx_mmu.c      | 143 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgx_mmu.h      |  49 +++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgx_mmu_test.c |  73 +++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 267 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgx_mmu.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgx_mmu.h
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgx_mmu_test.c

